  "_about": "HPN ATC transcript normaliser (GitHub #257; sizeup/atc_normalize.py): what speech-to-text writes for HPN's own words, mapped to how they are written. 'fixes': the approach fixes (FAA CIFP, data/airport/khpn_procedures.geojson) by what is heard for them, anywhere. 'fixes_in_context': spellings that are also ordinary words ('to do', 'harp'): only right after 'over', 'at', 'from', 'direct', 'via', 'crossing' ... A fix not listed is still recognised by its own ident, and by a close spelling in that context. 'telephony': airline and operator telephony as misheard, to its written form (data/atc/khpn_operators.csv, telephony_extra.csv). 'facility_misheard': words heard in place of 'Westchester' before 'Tower' / 'Ground' (a clipped first syllable, the ATC model's European airports). Lower case; one entry per mishearing.",
